From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simone Primarosa <simone.primarosa@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: prune dead nodes from raylet syncer to prevent reconnect broadcast storms

Stop a reconnecting raylet from replaying dead nodes' state to the cluster.

Each raylet keeps a syncer cluster view filled from GCS broadcasts about every
node. NodeManager::NodeRemoved drops a dead node from the scheduler's resource
manager but not from that view, and the syncer only forgets its direct peer. After
a reconnect the raylet resends the whole view, so the GCS, which already removed
those nodes, logs "received resource usage from unknown node id" and rebroadcasts
the stale entries to every node. In a long-lived cluster with heavy node churn one
reconnect replays every node that ever died, and the extra traffic breaks more
connections.

RaySyncer gains RemoveNode, which NodeRemoved now calls, so a dead node is never
resent. It also gains SetDeadNodeFilter: the GCS installs a filter backed by its node
manager's dead node set, and a message about a dead node is neither stored nor
rebroadcast. Either change alone stops the replay.

Upstream status: not yet reported to ray-project/ray.
